 opsadmin via /etc/cron.allow. The opsadmin user was created since it did not previously exist. Verified other users (e.g. antrieb) are denied crontab access while root/opsadmin succeed. Node1 was restarted via the mandatory protocol, and access control plus cron service health were confirmed intact post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (Ubuntu 16.04), cron package (vixie-cron based), and confirmed no /etc/cron.allow or /etc/cron.deny existed initially\",\"Created opsadmin user (uid 1001) since it did not exist on node1\",\"Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing 'root' and 'opsadmin' (owner root:root, mode 644), leaving /etc/cron.deny absent\",\"Verified antrieb (a non-listed user) is denied crontab access with 'not allowed to use this program' error\",\"Verified root and opsadmin can list/install/remove crontabs (installed and removed a test entry for opsadmin)\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and cron service state for node1\",\"Restarted node1 via 'sudo shutdown -r now' backgrounded so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned, confirmed boot_id changed proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart that cron.allow persisted, cron.service is active, and access enforcement (deny antrieb, allow opsadmin/root) still holds\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: cron config/service state before any changes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-656d956921db4170\",\"cmd-34ec39d402984c20\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed Ubuntu 16.04 with vixie-cron installed, no existing cron.allow/cron.deny, cron.service active, and no opsadmin user present initially\"},{\"requirement\":\"Created opsadmin user\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-56aa70650566448f\"],\"summary\":\"useradd -m -s /bin/bash opsadmin succeeded, id shows uid=1001(opsadmin)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only root and opsadmin allowed to schedule cron jobs (config applied)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-adbcd8498e8f487d\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote /etc/cron.allow with 'root' and 'opsadmin', confirmed file contents and no cron.deny present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof that non-listed users are denied and listed users are permitted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6f8d911f80f54249\",\"cmd-a7e9224e5984444f\"],\"summary\":\"antrieb user explicitly denied ('not allowed to use this program (crontab)'); opsadmin and root allowed (crontab -l returns 'no crontab for X' not a permission error); opsadmin successfully installed and removed a live crontab entry\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity, cron service, config)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2abdf71e858a48c5\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 2dffe735-a982-49f0-aa0a-19552507ae73, cron.service active, and /etc/cron.allow contents prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a0e84e8302a740b8\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sudo shutdown -r now' returned 'reboot acknowledged' immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node became unreachable then came back; changed boot identity proves real restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ecfa76615485449b\",\"cmd-27528370b8b74c0b\"],\"summary\":\"Connection refused immediately after reboot command, then exec succeeded again with new boot_id 66a01adf-057d-405c-a6b6-0d81c8e403ce (differs from pre-restart 2dffe735...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of cron service and access-control enforcement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2068c23e51f44587\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot: cron.service active, /etc/cron.allow still contains root/opsadmin, antrieb still denied crontab access, opsadmin still permitted\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, cron access is now restricted to root and opsadmin via /etc/cron.allow. The opsadmin user was created since it did not previously exist. Verified other users (e.g. antrieb) are denied crontab access while root/opsadmin succeed. Node1 was restarted via the mandatory protocol, and access control plus cron service health were confirmed intact post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (Ubuntu 16.04), cron package (vixie-cron based), and confirmed no /etc/cron.allow or /etc/cron.deny existed initially","Created opsadmin user (uid 1001) since it did not exist on node1","Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing 'root' and 'opsadmin' (owner root:root, mode 644), leaving /etc/cron.deny absent","Verified antrieb (a non-listed user) is denied crontab access with 'not allowed to use this program' error","Verified root and opsadmin can list/install/remove crontabs (installed and removed a test entry for opsadmin)","Captured baseline boot_id and cron service state for node1","Restarted node1 via 'sudo shutdown -r now' backgrounded so acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned, confirmed boot_id changed proving an actual restart","Re-verified post-restart that cron.allow persisted, cron.service is active, and access enforcement (deny antrieb, allow opsadmin/root) still holds"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: cron config/service state before any changes","command_ids":["cmd-656d956921db4170","cmd-34ec39d402984c20"],"summary":"Confirmed Ubuntu 16.04 with vixie-cron installed, no existing cron.allow/cron.deny, cron.service active, and no opsadmin user present initially"},{"requirement":"Created opsadmin user","command_ids":["cmd-56aa70650566448f"],"summary":"useradd -m -s /bin/bash opsadmin succeeded, id shows uid=1001(opsadmin)"},{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin allowed to schedule cron jobs (config applied)","command_ids":["cmd-adbcd8498e8f487d"],"summary":"Wrote /etc/cron.allow with 'root' and 'opsadmin', confirmed file contents and no cron.deny present"},{"requirement":"Proof that non-listed users are denied and listed users are permitted","command_ids":["cmd-6f8d911f80f54249","cmd-a7e9224e5984444f"],"summary":"antrieb user explicitly denied ('not allowed to use this program (crontab)'); opsadmin and root allowed (crontab -l returns 'no crontab for X' not a permission error); opsadmin successfully installed and removed a live crontab entry"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity, cron service, config)","command_ids":["cmd-2abdf71e858a48c5"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 2dffe735-a982-49f0-aa0a-19552507ae73, cron.service active, and /etc/cron.allow contents prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-a0e84e8302a740b8"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sudo shutdown -r now' returned 'reboot acknowledged' immediately"},{"requirement":"Node became unreachable then came back; changed boot identity proves real restart","command_ids":["cmd-ecfa76615485449b","cmd-27528370b8b74c0b"],"summary":"Connection refused immediately after reboot command, then exec succeeded again with new boot_id 66a01adf-057d-405c-a6b6-0d81c8e403ce (differs from pre-restart 2dffe735...)"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of cron service and access-control enforcement","command_ids":["cmd-2068c23e51f44587"],"summary":"After reboot: cron.service active, /etc/cron.allow still contains root/opsadmin, antrieb still denied crontab access, opsadmin still permitted"}]},"ttft_ms":1764,"type":"result","duration_ms":62769,"uuid":"bfee516a-14ef-4b95-85b9-072506eb1ce7","ttft_stream_ms":1607,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":1763,"queued_turn_count":0}
